[size=5][b]Simple Location Display[/b][/size]

A small popup in the bottom-left corner tells you where you are whenever you enter a new area. It uses the same box as the game's "It's getting late" message and fades out by itself.

[line]

[size=4][b]What it shows[/b][/size]
The popup uses the game's own names, so it follows your language setting with no extra files.
[list]
[*]Towns, shops, homes and other places with a name in the game data show that name.
[*]Farm buildings show the building's name, such as "Deluxe Coop".
[*]The Mines show "Mines" with "Level 12" on a second line. The Skull Cavern and the Volcano do the same, and the number matches the one the game draws in the top-left corner.
[*]A few places the game never names, such as the Night Market and some Ginger Island rooms, use text the game already translates.
[*]Locations added by other mods show the name the mod gave them. If a mod gave none, the popup tries the warp name from CJB Cheats Menu (when you have it), and after that a readable version of the internal name.
[/list]
A popup that would appear during a cutscene waits until the cutscene ends.

[line]

[size=4][b]Install[/b][/size]
[list=1]
[*]Install SMAPI 4.2.1 or newer.
[*]Unzip the download and put the SimpleLocationDisplay folder in Stardew Valley/Mods.
[*]Optional: install Generic Mod Config Menu to change settings in game.
[/list]
Needs Stardew Valley 1.6.9 or newer.

[b]Updating from 1.x:[/b] replace the old SimpleLocationDisplay folder with the new one. Your config.json carries over and needs no edits. Two things look different in 2.0: Mines, Skull Cavern and Volcano popups put the level on a second line, and three translation keys that could no longer be reached were removed (location.Temp, location.BathHouse_Entry, location.UndergroundMine). The full list is on the GitHub changelog.

[line]

[size=4][b]Settings[/b][/size]
Open the config menu from the title screen or the game menu, or edit config.json in the mod folder.
[list]
[*][b]EnableMod[/b] (default true): turns the popups on or off.
[*][b]NotificationDuration[/b] (default 3500): how long the popup stays, in milliseconds, between 1000 and 10000.
[*][b]ShowOnSaveLoad[/b] (default true): also shows the popup for the place you start in when you load a save.
[*][b]ShowZeroAsL0[/b] (default false): shows level 0 of a dungeon as "L0" instead of leaving the number off.
[*][b]HiddenLocations[/b] (default empty): places that never get a popup. Use an internal location name or the text the popup shows. In the config menu it is a comma-separated box.
[*][b]EnableDebugLogging[/b] (default false): writes extra detail about each popup to the SMAPI log.
[/list]

[line]

[size=4][b]Location mods[/b][/size]
I checked the popup in a save with Stardew Valley Expanded 1.15.11, Ridgeside Village 2.5.17 and East Scarp Remastered 3.0.9 loaded, on Stardew Valley 1.6.15 with SMAPI 4.5.2. The popup text was worked out for all 367 locations in that world with no errors. All three mods give most of their places a display name, which the popup uses, and cutscenes in them wait as described above. Generic Mod Config Menu and CJB Cheats Menu are optional. Split-screen players each keep their own popup, but I have not run a live multiplayer or split-screen session. For places without a name, the popup falls back to a readable name, so Custom_FrontierFarm_HiddenCave becomes "Frontier Farm Hidden Cave", and a character's name before a place word gets a possessive, so Custom_MarnieShed reads "Marnie's Shed". Rooms that mods use to park characters (names with WarpRoom in them) get no popup.

[b]For mod authors:[/b] the best fix is to set DisplayName on your location in Data/Locations. If you cannot, edit the asset Mods/Kkthnx.SimpleLocationDisplay/Names with Content Patcher. The key is the location name and the value is the text. A blank value hides the popup for that location. The README on GitHub has an example.

[line]

[size=4][b]Translations[/b][/size]
The mod carries a Spanish file, and for each of the game's other languages the names of the Skull Cavern, the Cellar and the Quarry Mine, taken from the game's own text in that language. I checked the popup in all twelve languages in game. The Casino has no text in the game to take a word from, so it stays English until someone translates it. Everything else comes from the game, or falls back to English. If a place shows a raw name, stand in it and type [b]debug_location[/b] in the SMAPI console, then post the line it prints.

[line]

[size=4][b]Reporting bugs[/b][/size]
Post on the Bugs tab with a SMAPI log from smapi.io/log and the line that debug_location prints while you stand in the place. If you can, say whether it still happens with only SMAPI and this mod installed.

